@* HealthTips.cshtml - maternal and newborn health education article cards. *@
@{
    Layout = "_PublicLayout";
    ViewData["Title"] = "Health Tips";
}

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="chip chip-butter">Health Education</span>
    <h1>Trusted maternal &amp; newborn health tips</h1>
    <p>Simple, practical guidance for expectant mothers, families, and village health volunteers across every stage of pregnancy and infancy.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container grid-3">
    <article class="pub-card reveal">
      <img src="~/images/hero-care.jpg" alt="Hands gently cradling newborn baby feet" class="card-photo" />
      <span class="chip chip-sage">First Trimester</span>
      <h3>Start folic acid &amp; register before 12 weeks</h3>
      <p>Early registration ensures accurate EDD calculation and allows your clinic to check baseline hemoglobin, blood group, and blood pressure right away.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="pub-card reveal">
      <img src="~/images/baby-feet.jpg" alt="Warm sunlight on tiny newborn feet" class="card-photo" />
      <span class="chip chip-butter">Nutrition</span>
      <h3>Iron-rich meals to prevent anaemia</h3>
      <p>Pair green leafy vegetables, jaggery, and lentils with vitamin C (lemon or amla) to boost iron absorption, and take prescribed IFA tablets daily after meals.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="pub-card reveal">
      <img src="~/images/newborn-scale.jpg" alt="Clinical check-up for newborn" class="card-photo" />
      <span class="chip chip-rose">Warning Signs</span>
      <h3>When to visit the clinic immediately</h3>
      <p>Seek medical care right away for severe headaches, blurred vision, sudden swelling of face or hands, reduced baby movement, fever, or any bleeding.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="pub-card reveal">
      <img src="~/images/newborn-sleep.jpg" alt="Sleeping newborn close-up" class="card-photo" />
      <span class="chip chip-sage">Second Trimester</span>
      <h3>Never skip your mid-pregnancy ANC visit</h3>
      <p>Between weeks 14 and 26, monitoring blood pressure and blood sugar helps detect gestational hypertension and diabetes well before complications arise.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="pub-card reveal">
      <img src="~/images/baby-crib.jpg" alt="Baby resting peacefully in crib" class="card-photo" />
      <span class="chip chip-butter">Birth Preparedness</span>
      <h3>Plan for a safe institutional delivery</h3>
      <p>By week 32, confirm your hospital or PHC, arrange emergency transport, pack your ANC health card, and keep your family's emergency contacts handy.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="pub-card reveal">
      <img src="~/images/newborn-scale.jpg" alt="Newborn vaccination and postnatal check" class="card-photo" />
      <span class="chip chip-sage">Newborn Care</span>
      <h3>Keep up with the 7 UIP vaccine milestones</h3>
      <p>Timely doses at birth, 6 weeks, 10 weeks, 14 weeks, and 9 months build lifelong immunity against tuberculosis, polio, hepatitis B, diphtheria, and measles.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
